 "Now verify against a real local server returning 503 twice, then 200; and always-503; and 404.\n`WeatherClient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It tries up to 3 times in total and waits longer before each retry: 0.5s, then 1s. I tested it against a real local HTTP server:\n\n- **503 twice, then 200:** returns the data on the 3rd request.\n- **503 every time:** raises the 503 `HTTPError` after 3 requests.\n- **404:** raises right away after 1 request, with no retry.\n\nDetails:\n- Only `HTTPError` with code 503 is retried. Other HTTP errors, network errors and timeouts are raised immediately, as before.\n- I added two constructor options, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5` (seconds). The tests used `backoff=0.01` so they ran quickly. Existing calls to `WeatherClient(base_url, timeout)` work unchanged.\n- The server's `Retry-After` header is not used; the wait is always the fixed backoff.\n- I didn't add a test file because the repo has no test setup; the test above was a one-off script.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "provider_error": "Anthropic stream stalled while waiting for the next event", "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 3, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 35616, "requests_cache_write": 178012, "requests_cost_usd": 0.9325792, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1767, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial6", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 70, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:39:21.416007+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 146.236, "t_checker_s": 2.536, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir